From e0aaab8eb83bd2deab5a48213d3481c4f230149f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:36:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: expose typed node shutdown and RPC stop lifecycle
 events

Convert five shutdown/RPC lifecycle producers without changing their
category, level, readable text, exception branches or shutdown order.
Existing SourceFunction and Error keys snapshot the values safely;
no public API or field registry changes are needed. PID removal failure
remains Warning, while missing PID and shutdown progress remain Info.
RPC stop remains debug/RPC and does not become default output.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py 0.51.0, from the parent checkout):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/node-shutdown-lifecycle.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/node-shutdown-applied.json --apply
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/init.cpp

Explicit support: add a reviewed wallet-less functional fixture for
actual JSON fields, text, levels and category. It removes only its own
PID file to exercise the missing-file branch, then substitutes a nonempty
owned PID directory to exercise the existing caught filesystem error.
No production data, browser, wallet or protocol behavior is touched.

Source checks: converter15 fixtures/idempotence, production event lint302,
Ruff0.15.8 and whitespace pass. Native build and actual functional gates
are pending separate receipts, not inferred from source checks.
Shared eCash owner; V2 inherits unchanged.
